{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-35754" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What are the pivot columns of the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044251/state.json" "file_sha256" "9141e26300f57a32e0acc838106176dd4d7ed630ac028a09511bb8c3a289bb46"} {"question" "q-35754" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to convert $A$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $A$ has $2$ pivots. In particular, the pivot columns are the $1$st and $2$nd columns." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044251/state.json" "file_sha256" "9141e26300f57a32e0acc838106176dd4d7ed630ac028a09511bb8c3a289bb46"} {"question" "q-35754" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044251/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "68f8816ea43ac3c3244e51fc9497ca2fffb25c4763b1771e2ba195e86de5fbd2"} {"question" "q-35754" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044251/state.json" "file_sha256" "9141e26300f57a32e0acc838106176dd4d7ed630ac028a09511bb8c3a289bb46"} {"question" "q-35754" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$1$st and $2$nd only"] ["text" "$1$st only"] ["text" "$1$st, $2$nd, and $3$rd"] ["text" "$2$nd only"] ["text" "$3$rd only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044251/state.json" "file_sha256" "9141e26300f57a32e0acc838106176dd4d7ed630ac028a09511bb8c3a289bb46"} {"question" "q-35754" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$1$st and $2$nd only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044251/state.json" "file_sha256" "9141e26300f57a32e0acc838106176dd4d7ed630ac028a09511bb8c3a289bb46"} {"question" "q-35757" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What are the pivot columns of the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044251/state.json" "file_sha256" "9141e26300f57a32e0acc838106176dd4d7ed630ac028a09511bb8c3a289bb46"} {"question" "q-35757" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to convert $A$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $A$ has $3$ pivots. In particular, the pivot columns are the $1$st, $2$nd, and $4$th columns." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044251/state.json" "file_sha256" "9141e26300f57a32e0acc838106176dd4d7ed630ac028a09511bb8c3a289bb46"} {"question" "q-35757" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044251/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "68f8816ea43ac3c3244e51fc9497ca2fffb25c4763b1771e2ba195e86de5fbd2"} {"question" "q-35757" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044251/state.json" "file_sha256" "9141e26300f57a32e0acc838106176dd4d7ed630ac028a09511bb8c3a289bb46"} {"question" "q-35757" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$1$st and $2$nd only"] ["text" "$1$st, $2$nd, and $4$th only"] ["text" "$2$nd and $3$rd only"] ["text" "$3$rd and $4$th only"] ["text" "$3$rd only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044251/state.json" "file_sha256" "9141e26300f57a32e0acc838106176dd4d7ed630ac028a09511bb8c3a289bb46"} {"question" "q-35757" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$1$st, $2$nd, and $4$th only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044251/state.json" "file_sha256" "9141e26300f57a32e0acc838106176dd4d7ed630ac028a09511bb8c3a289bb46"} {"question" "q-73620" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The row echelon form matrix $A$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044251/state.json" "file_sha256" "9141e26300f57a32e0acc838106176dd4d7ed630ac028a09511bb8c3a289bb46"} {"question" "q-73620" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $A$ has $3$ pivots in the $1$st, $2$nd and $4$th columns:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot columns are the $3$rd and $5$th columns." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044251/state.json" "file_sha256" "9141e26300f57a32e0acc838106176dd4d7ed630ac028a09511bb8c3a289bb46"} {"question" "q-73620" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044251/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "68f8816ea43ac3c3244e51fc9497ca2fffb25c4763b1771e2ba195e86de5fbd2"} {"question" "q-73620" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044251/state.json" "file_sha256" "9141e26300f57a32e0acc838106176dd4d7ed630ac028a09511bb8c3a289bb46"} {"question" "q-73620" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$2$nd, $3$rd, and $5$th only"] ["text" "$3$rd and $5$th only"] ["text" "$3$rd only"] ["text" "$3$rd, $4$th, and $5$th only"] ["text" "$5$th only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044251/state.json" "file_sha256" "9141e26300f57a32e0acc838106176dd4d7ed630ac028a09511bb8c3a289bb46"} {"question" "q-73620" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$3$rd and $5$th only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044251/state.json" "file_sha256" "9141e26300f57a32e0acc838106176dd4d7ed630ac028a09511bb8c3a289bb46"} {"question" "q-73628" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine the number of pivot columns of the matrix $B,$ given by\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 4 & -5 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 3 & -6 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044251/state.json" "file_sha256" "9141e26300f57a32e0acc838106176dd4d7ed630ac028a09511bb8c3a289bb46"} {"question" "q-73628" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to convert $B$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 4 & -5 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 3 & -6 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 4 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & -8 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $B$ has $4$ pivots, and therefore the number of pivot columns is $4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044251/state.json" "file_sha256" "9141e26300f57a32e0acc838106176dd4d7ed630ac028a09511bb8c3a289bb46"} {"question" "q-73628" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044251/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "68f8816ea43ac3c3244e51fc9497ca2fffb25c4763b1771e2ba195e86de5fbd2"} {"question" "q-73628" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Develo